WEBVTT

00:02:57.436 --> 00:03:01.036
I actually started thinking
with renewed clarity about life

00:03:01.076 --> 00:03:03.676
and work and COVID

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:05.556
and all the things that mattered.

00:03:06.516 --> 00:03:10.396
In Bronnie Ware's book
"The Top Five Regrets of the Dying,"

00:03:10.436 --> 00:03:13.516
Bronnie will tell you
the second-biggest regret

00:03:13.556 --> 00:03:16.596
is "I wish I hadn't spent
so much time in the office."

00:03:17.436 --> 00:03:19.556
But you don't need me to tell you that.

00:03:19.596 --> 00:03:22.236
You know what's important
on your deathbed,

00:03:22.236 --> 00:03:24.476
the love of friends and family,

00:03:24.516 --> 00:03:26.916
the legacy you're leaving behind,

00:03:26.956 --> 00:03:30.076
knowing that you've done things
that made you happy,